Trademark and Attribution Notice
--------------------------------

vinOS is an independent Linux distribution based on Arch Linux. vinOS
is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by the Arch Linux
project.

"Arch Linux" and the Arch Linux logo (the blue triangle) are
trademarks of the Arch Linux team. vinOS does not use the Arch Linux
name or logo as part of its own identity. Where the string "arch"
appears in vinOS (e.g. `ID_LIKE=arch` in `/etc/os-release`, or the
on-medium `install_dir=arch`), it is used descriptively to signal
Arch-derivation in the standard Linux-vendor way, not as branding.

vinOS is built from the archiso profile shipped by the Arch Linux
project. The upstream archiso profile is available at
<https://gitlab.archlinux.org/archlinux/archiso> and licensed under
the GNU General Public License v3. Modifications to that profile are
retained under the same license.


Third-party components
----------------------

vinOS installs and redistributes software packages from:

  - the Arch Linux official repositories (core, extra, multilib);
  - the Arch User Repository (AUR), built via `iso/aur-build.sh`;
  - upstream vendors (e.g. 1Password, Spotify, Obsidian) whose
    packages are repackaged by the corresponding AUR PKGBUILDs.

Each individual package retains its own license and copyright as
declared by its upstream author. vinOS makes no additional claim of
ownership over redistributed third-party software. See each
installed package's own `LICENSE` (typically under
`/usr/share/licenses/<pkgname>/`) for details.
